# CV notes

Lines to lift into a CV or a cover letter, grouped by skill. Each ends with its evidence: a claim
of the public ledger (`claim`), a metric of the public model registry (`registry`), or a file of the
repository. `strata ledger check` fails if a line has no evidence, if its evidence does not exist,
or if a number in it was typed by hand.

Numbers come only from allow-listed claims, computed on the real extract and published with their
sample size and period. The quality of the models trained on the real extract is published in
`metrics_only` mode: aggregate metrics with their intervals, never a score, a reason or a feature
importance. The public registry holds models trained on synthetic data, which show that a method
runs, never how well it predicts.

## The project

- Built Strata, an end-to-end analytics pipeline for multi-channel retail-banking event data, from
  typed contracts to a dashboard, run on an anonymised extract of {{ n("channel_mix") }} bank
  clients and, for everyone else, on a synthetic generator of the same schema.
  Evidence: claim `channel_mix`; [the architecture](../ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Data engineering

- Built a typed ingestion layer with schema contracts and reconciliation checks that flags exact
  repeat rows instead of guessing, and surfaced a silently empty join in the original analysis.
  Evidence: [the contracts](../strata/contracts/specs.py); [the legacy bugs](../legacy/README.md).
- Modelled three banking channels into a dbt warehouse on DuckDB, every model and seed tested, with
  window-function features for recency, rolling sums and monthly channel states, and a test that
  rebuilds the features after changing every later event to prove that no feature reads past its
  cutoff.
  Evidence: [the dbt project](../dbt/dbt_project.yml); [the leakage test](../tests/test_models.py).
- Made the pipeline source-agnostic: any client-and-events extract plugs in through a mapping file,
  proven by a property-based test that maps a generated alien schema onto the same marts.
  Evidence: [the mapping layer](../mappings/README.md); [the alien schema](../tests/alien.py).

## Evidence and statistics

- Designed an evidence ledger where every number in the documentation is generated from a
  registered, bootstrapped claim and CI fails on drift, plus a stratification check that showed a
  headline retention finding reversing once activity level was controlled.
  Evidence: claim `silence_by_channel`; [the ledger check](../strata/ledger/check.py).
