- Found that {{ ledger("channel_mix", "share_mixed") }} of the bank's sampled clients combine the
  branch with a digital channel and {{ ledger("channel_mix", "share_branch_only") }} use only the
  branch, a share that grows from {{ ledger("age_digital_divide", "branch_only_" ~ youngest[1]) }}
  in the {{ youngest[0] }} age band to {{ ledger("age_digital_divide", "branch_only_" ~ oldest[1]) }}
  in the {{ oldest[0] }} band.
  Evidence: claim `channel_mix`; claim `age_digital_divide`.
- Measured card spend concentration (Gini {{ ledger("spend_concentration", "gini") }}) and an excess
  of leading nines in card purchase amounts of {{ ledger("benford_purchases", "digit_9_excess") }}
  against Benford's law, the mark of psychological pricing.
  Evidence: claim `spend_concentration`; claim `benford_purchases`.
- Fitted negative-binomial and Bayesian calendar models of daily transactions with Ramadan, Eid and
  salary-day effects, and a Dirichlet-posterior channel Markov chain that simulates branch load
  under migration policies with uncertainty bands.
  Evidence: [the calendar method](methods/calendar.md); [the Markov method](methods/markov.md).

## Machine learning

- Predicted ninety-day client silence with time-based validation, comparing a logistic GLM against a
  tuned LightGBM with isotonic and Platt calibration and SHAP reasons: on a later cutoff of the real
  extract the served score reached a Brier score of {{ ledger("silence_model_quality", "brier") }}
  ({{ ci("silence_model_quality", "brier") }}), a calibration error of
  {{ ledger("silence_model_quality", "calibration_error") }} and a lift of
  {{ ledger("silence_model_quality", "lift_at_10") }} in the top tenth of scores, on
  {{ n("silence_model_quality") }} clients.
  Evidence: claim `silence_model_quality`; registry `silence.headline.backtests`;
  [the silence model card](model_cards/silence.md).
- Profiled behavioural segments selected by BIC whose assignment reproduces with a bootstrap
  stability (mean adjusted Rand index) of {{ ledger("segment_stability", "mean_ari") }}
  ({{ ci("segment_stability", "mean_ari") }}) on the real extract.
  Evidence: claim `segment_stability`; [the segments model card](model_cards/segments.md).
- Built a transaction-monitoring triage layer combining configurable rules (structuring, velocity,
  pass-through) with Isolation Forest and empirical-Bayes amount models, ranked by an alert budget
  and improved by analyst feedback.
  Evidence: [the rules](../strata/models/anomaly/rules.yaml); [the monitoring method](methods/anomaly.md).
- Generated a differentially private synthetic twin of the client table whose fidelity and
  membership-inference risk are measured before any use.
  Evidence: [the twin](../strata/synthetic/twin.py); [its decision record](adr/0013-private-twin.md).

## Software and product

- Served risk scores, segments, alerts and a policy simulator through a FastAPI service with
  PostgreSQL feedback storage, Alembic migrations and Prometheus metrics, packaged with Docker
  Compose.
  Evidence: [the API](../strata/api/app.py); [the Compose file](../docker-compose.yml).
- Designed a nine-page analytics dashboard in React and TypeScript (customer profiles, segments, risk,
  alerts, what-if simulator) with Storybook-documented components and accessibility checks.
  Evidence: [the dashboard](../apps/dashboard/src/App.tsx); [the smoke tests](../apps/dashboard/e2e/smoke.spec.ts).
- Orchestrated ingestion, dbt, training, evaluation and reporting as an Airflow DAG, with a gate that
  stops the run when a model was trained on other data or does no better than chance.
  Evidence: [the DAG](../orchestration/airflow/dags/strata_daily.py); [the gate](../strata/models/evaluate.py).
- Engineered a privacy boundary for confidential bank data: zones, a pre-commit guard that learns
  the shape of real identifiers without ever echoing one, an allow-list with a minimum group size,
  and verdict-only publication for findings whose numbers must stay private.
  Evidence: [the guard](../strata/privacy_guard.py); [the privacy notes](../PRIVACY.md); claim `silence_by_channel`.
